# No agent attribution in git or pull requests

Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Generated with`, or any agent, tool, or model name to commit messages, squash or merge commit bodies, or pull request titles or bodies.

Author and committer are already set in the local git config. Never change them.

Workers must not commit at all unless the task explicitly says to commit.

Right after every commit, run `git log -1 --format=%B`. If that message contains `Co-authored-by`, `Generated with`, or any agent, tool, or model attribution, amend it with `git commit --amend -F` after writing a cleaned message file that strips those lines.

Never stage `plans/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`, `.agents/`, `.agentkit/`, `.codex/`, `.devin/`, or `.env*`.
